<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>€561 Billion and Still Not Enough: Germany's 2027 Budget Exposes a Coalition on the Brink</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fae5191bed023282f793218a266279ffa829f6eb0daf78be8ee6ec4b06fee2ed</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664--c8b0f8b87743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/€561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget for 2027 has reached new highs, and pension funds, defense spending and a weak economy are increasing the pressure. At the same time, tensions are mounting within the government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: 'We can no longer afford everything,' Merz says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd27c163b4b3688f05d497d7f9c26076e97f8cb891ee004ba12dc0ad61a3805a</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795--0bc2dba71ae9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German chancellor has warned tax revenue means a tighter budget for 2027 and beyond. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier is in Kenya for the final leg of his Africa tour.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Wadephul 'shocked' by Trump's Nvidia intervention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15055c4c71dccd5bfa7a21777cc0cf76edfbf807990212062314ec170851aa92</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T13:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954--71b26658a53e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-wadephul-shocked-by-trump-s-nvidia-intervention/a-80033954?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German foreign minister has criticized Donald Trump's interference in the chip-maker's economic activities. Jensen Huang was brought back after stepping down as Nvidia CEO amid multiple scandals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU imposes import quotas for hybrid vehicles from China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bc9425cfb2cb4fb675fe7807122ce1059a4b927c0eb6e486cc240401f77ef04</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981--7d148967ab4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is trying to protect its own car manufacturers from what it called "overcapacity" in China. Carmakers in the bloc, especially in Germany, have been lagging behind their Chinese rivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen begins wage talks with IG Metall union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76e1ada2aa9fda5639b0a78815760b787529f1342e753b6b3dfc6ba18375cdc4</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306--34d90226a697.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's largest labor union IG Metall and automaker Volkswagen are holding wage negotiations, as the company looks to embark on cost-cutting measures. Meanwhile, Germany's president is in Ghana. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German firms eye Africa as global trade shocks hit traditional markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4488107a1128b2a9a94e5c83bf1f202781382f7b62f60a1c9d531670c15884e6</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671--b64160bb0ab9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German businesses are optimistic about Africa, but Berlin's cautious approach to risk is holding them back from cashing in on the opportunities that their competitors from countries like the UAE and Turkey are seizing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey prospect Max Calce follows Leon Draisaitl's path, leaving Mannheim for Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31c976874cd6aad0f0339a4e6271fa2ad6363fd9e1b31b17f3627fe5682e9216</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458--4ca1ab8cf6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The player widely seen as Germany's biggest ice hockey talent to come along in years is leaving the country's top professional league for Canada – changing tracks in his bid to make it to the NHL.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women's football team take stand against domestic violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7081b4b31ae8e2f4c099a0e1364b4d315580d16d5c50422453e1991770632351</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974--84aba926a54f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-s-football-team-take-stand-against-domestic-violence/a-70907974?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's women's football team are to wear UN Women badges in games against Argentina and Peru, as domestic violence hits a record high in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German auto workers on back foot as costs, competition bite</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98ba03d0f7fffe7363186c9789e24fd8d5cdb1c65828ddcaef4259c8a6c74592</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111--50a0a19d14b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-auto-workers-on-back-foot-as-costs-competition-bite/a-80036111?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German auto workers profited during the industry's boom years, but are now increasingly being asked to trade past gains for future job security.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Domestic violence soars to record high in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be53cf9121979c6506ef5aa3fbd885f0be49583e2e426b6d4edc7c8f65160fbe</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678--cb6cf80357ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/domestic-violence-soars-to-record-high-in-germany/a-80041678?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Every three days in Germany, a man kills his wife or ex-partner. Every 10 minutes, the police record a sexual offense against a woman. "A shocking finding," according to Justice Minister Stefanie Hubig.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d92f110b4ed743d5415d6b0f99b22f2d6a1ea679327a3952385d59a6ee586c8</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T16:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852--1abf02560b4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-s-bid-for-nato-membership-and-more-air-defense-remains-controversial/a-80029852?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is calling for the rapid acceptance of his country into NATO. However, the necessary unanimity for this is lacking, as shown during the NATO Parliamentary Assembly in Berlin.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'I've lost her forever' — Why German voice actors are refusing to sign Netflix's AI contract</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a516151866247077fdeae5b11478785fcf04d17c193bd7a110c6a28ce5a20aa6</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381--da3277b6e37b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/i-ve-lost-her-forever-why-german-voice-actors-are-refusing-to-sign-netflix-s-ai-contract/a-80004381?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For decades, Germans have known Hollywood's biggest stars through the same familiar voices. Now an AI clause in Netflix contracts is splitting the industry over whether it protects performers or exposes them.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6dcac703ee114ca2c514fd6c279d73bdb58614773c4b69b94d89e123100b74</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-26T08:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
